{\citet[458--459]{gvdb} suggested Taxus baccata L., but that tree is endemic to the Mediterraenean and not  South Asia. \cite{poud-2013} show that T. contorta Griff., T mairei (Lem\'ee \& L\'ev.) and T. wallichiana Zucc.\ are distributed in the Hindu Kush - Himalaya region.  The Nepalese name Thuṇeraka is etymologically cognate with the Sanskrit name.  T. contorta is of medicinal importance, so its common name is used here}


